  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been wanting to make a sort of \"avatar inventory system\", in this case for a Ben 10-themed avatar that can switch between different avatars, but I cannot keep it within reasonable performance metrics without it being an avatar switch triggered either through OSC or an Animator State Behaviour. (since the alternative would be having all avatars in one and constraining their bone rotations, very bad)\nI understand this could be exploited with API call spamming, so a timeout would definitely be expected.\nTL;DR\nI wanna make a Ben 10 Omnitrix watch but also don't want to force people to load 10 avatars in one. (plus I refuse to upload a VeryPoor avatar ^^\")",
